"}, "name": "Public Tour - 0 reg 1hr close - Default"}, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 9250, "description": "## Duration, Distance, Terrain\n1.5 hours\n1.6 miles at a moderate walking pace, stopping at various sites along the tour\nMostly flat surfaces and little to no inclines\n## About\nFew are unfamiliar with the famous “Nashville Wings” done by Kelsey Montague. Did you know one of her illustrations is right here in Boston, “Balloons Over Boston/What Lifts You”? The walk from Copley Square through the South End is full of underappreciated and unknown artwork. On this tour, experience the wonder of the “Betances Mural” to the deeply symbolic work of Pablo Eduardo. One need not know anything about art, only enjoy beauty in its many forms, to love this tour. “Step on Board” as we discover these hidden gems (bring your camera)!\n## Meeting location:\nMeet your guide at the Johnson Entrance to the Boston Public Library on Boylston Street\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest Accessible MBTA Station: Copley (Green Line)\n## What to bring\nComfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Discover a trove of unknown and underappreciated works of art", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/378556/images/933174/", "pk": 933174, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/secSMb5Rxeo1AAwqik45", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/secSMb5Rxeo1AAwqik45", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/"}, "item": {"cls": "Item